  <header class="doc-hero">
    <p class="page-head__eyebrow">Legal</p>
    <h1>Cookie Notice</h1>
    <p class="lead">WhereITis sets three short-lived cookies, all needed to sign you in and keep account actions secure. This page tells you what they are and how to remove them.</p>
  </header>
  <%- include('../partials/docNav', { current: 'cookies' }) %>

  <div class="doc-layout">
    <aside class="doc-toc" aria-label="On this page">
      <p class="doc-toc__title">On this page</p>
      <ol><li><a href="#s-1">The cookies we set</a></li><li><a href="#s-2">What we do NOT set</a></li><li><a href="#s-3">How to clear the cookies</a></li><li><a href="#s-4">What happens if we add cookies later</a></li></ol>
    </aside>
    <article class="doc-body">

  <h2 id="s-1">The cookies we set</h2>
  <div class="table-wrap">
    <table class="table">
      <thead><tr><th>Name</th><th>Where it is used</th><th>What it holds</th><th>Lifetime</th><th>Flags</th></tr></thead>
      <tbody>
        <tr>
          <td><code>whereitis_id</code></td>
          <td>Across the whole site, to show your account and allow signed-in actions</td>
          <td>A signed value that points at your row in the users table. No
          personal data can be read from the cookie itself.</td>
          <td>30 minutes</td>
          <td>HttpOnly, SameSite=Lax, Secure in production</td>
        </tr>
        <tr>
          <td><code>whereitis_pwreset</code></td>
          <td>Only while you are resetting a forgotten password</td>
          <td>A signed, short-lived pointer to the pending reset</td>
          <td>10 minutes</td>
          <td>HttpOnly, SameSite=Lax, Secure in production</td>
        </tr>
        <tr>
          <td><code>whereitis_verifywait</code></td>
          <td>Only on the "check your email" page after registering</td>
          <td>A signed, short-lived helper so the page knows which account you just created</td>
          <td>24 hours</td>
          <td>HttpOnly, SameSite=Lax, Secure in production</td>
        </tr>
      </tbody>
    </table>
  </div>

  <h2 id="s-2">What we do NOT set</h2>
  <ul>
    <li>No analytics cookies</li>
    <li>No advertising cookies</li>
    <li>No third-party cookies set by WhereITis itself</li>
    <li>No tracking pixels</li>
  </ul>
  <p class="muted">If you choose <strong>Continue with Google</strong>, Google may set its own cookies on
  <code>accounts.google.com</code> to keep you signed in to your Google Account. Those are controlled by Google,
  not by WhereITis, and our three cookies above are unchanged.</p>

  <h2 id="s-3">How to clear the cookie</h2>
  <p>Sign out of My Reports (the button on that page clears the cookie), or clear
  cookies for this site through your browser's settings. After clearing, you will
  need to sign in again.</p>

  <h2 id="s-4">What happens if we add cookies later</h2>
  <p>Any future cookie must be added to this page before it is deployed. If you
  notice a cookie not listed here, report it to the IT office — that is a bug.</p>

      <aside class="doc-help">
        <strong>Still have a question?</strong>
        <span>Visit the IT office or any staff member, or read the <a href="/help">User guide</a>.</span>
      </aside>
    </article>
  </div>
</main>

